## UI Quality: avoid the "AI aesthetic"

AI-generated UI has recognizable tells. For any UI work reject the generic default in favour of this template's design tokens (`@theme inline` + `:root` / `.dark` HSL vars in `app/globals.css`). This is a public, SEO-facing template, so "AI slop" output ships into every fork.

- **Palette**: brand is **blue** (`--primary` = `hsl(221.2 83.2% 53.3%)`) on slate neutrals (`--secondary` / `--muted` / `--accent`), `--destructive` red. Use semantic classes (`bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `bg-muted`, `border-border`, `ring-ring`), never raw `purple-*` / `indigo-*` or arbitrary hex.
- **Gradients**: none in `@theme`; keep surfaces flat. `tw-animate-css` is the only sanctioned animation layer, no hand-rolled gradient washes or glows.
- **Radius**: tokens derive from `--radius: 0.5rem` (`--radius-sm` / `-md` / `-lg`). Vary radius by hierarchy; no `rounded-2xl` / `rounded-full` on every card and button.
- **Layout**: content-first and priority-driven (the H1 and copy carry ranking weight), not a decorative hero followed by a uniform grid of identical cards.
- **Copy**: realistic strings from `messages/<locale>.json` (next-intl), never lorem-ipsum; real length surfaces wrapping, overflow and truncation during dev.
- **Padding & shadows**: no shadow tokens exist in `@theme`; use `shadow-*` sparingly (or `border-border` separation) and the spacing scale, not blanket oversized padding.
- **Dark mode only, in practice**: `app/layout.tsx` hardcodes `className="... dark"` on `<html>` and no theme toggle exists, so `.dark` is always applied and the `:root` (light) tokens never render. Verify new surfaces against the `.dark` values.
- **Baseline APIs only**: stick to Baseline "Widely available" (`:has()`, container queries, `<dialog>`, `scroll-snap`, view-transitions); a "Newly available" API (e.g. `scheduler.yield()`) needs a fallback.

## Interaction & base-layer states (binding)

- **States must be PERCEPTIBLY DISTINCT, not merely present.** A hover / active / focus / selection colour must not resolve to about the element's own default or background colour. Seen in the wild: a base link colour equal to its `hover:` colour (only the cursor changes); a `::selection` highlight built on a near-background token (invisible selection). Chrome/nav links default to a neutral (`text-muted-foreground`) so the `hover:text-primary` shift shows.
- **Compound states must stay COHERENT.** When two states co-occur (focus+invalid, hover+selected, disabled+focus) the more urgent one owns the shared channel (an invalid field recolours its focus ring, `aria-invalid:focus-visible:ring-destructive`; disabled cancels hover). Check state PAIRS, not just singles.
- **Base-layer globals** (`::selection`, base links, `:focus-visible`) are built on `--primary` / `--ring`, never on quiet near-background tokens (`--muted`, a slate-3-style `--accent`). For `::selection` use `background-color: hsl(var(--primary)); color: hsl(var(--primary-foreground));`.

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML first; ARIA only where needed (`role="status"` + `aria-live="polite"` for loading, `role="alert"` + `aria-live="assertive"` for critical errors); keyboard navigation always; shadcn/ui components carry their own a11y.
- **A public route is scanned at runtime**: the page-level spec that loads it calls `expectNoSevereA11yViolations(page)` from `@/e2e/support/a11y` after its readiness assertion (serious and critical fail, `target-size` on). Add that one call, never a new `test()`.

## SEO and i18n usage

- Metadata API, `generateMetadata`, `app/sitemap.ts` and `app/robots.ts`: `routing.mdc` and `react-patterns.mdc`. Structured data goes in `metadata.other['application/ld+json']`.
- next-intl SSR, no `public/locales/*`: `messages/<locale>.json` is the single source (flat namespaces `common`, `errors`, `home`, `meta`, …); config lives in root `i18n/` (`routing.ts`, `request.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `request-locale.ts`). `global.d.ts` augments next-intl's `AppConfig`, so `t('key')` is checked at compile time. Server: `getTranslations('home')` from `next-intl/server`; client: `useTranslations('home')`.
- Locale set is `['en']`; adding a language is `README.md` § Adding Languages (`AGENTS.md` invariant 5).
